      "description": "<cognition:model_facing_content> writes the model-facing content of a turn, each block indented two spaces per level and the blocks joined by newlines, most stable first: the recent turns (a cognition:recalled holding an uncounted recent of memory:turn lines), the situation (the environment block, then a cognition:acted of what earlier stages already did), the recalled episodes and directives (a cognition:recalled), the stimulus, when given, as the root element of its own block (tagged by its payload's type, stamped stimulus:event, then stimulus:id, stimulus:source and stimulus:target when set), then the feedback; systemlocation receives the instructions then the self block (a persona element), and failurelocation null.",
